## Producer Configuration Profiles

```java
// High-durability producer (financial data, orders)
@Bean
public ProducerFactory<String, Object> durableProducerFactory() {
    Map<String, Object> config = new HashMap<>();
    config.put(ProducerConfig.BOOTSTRAP_SERVERS_CONFIG, "kafka:9092");
    config.put(ProducerConfig.KEY_SERIALIZER_CLASS_CONFIG, StringSerializer.class);
    config.put(ProducerConfig.VALUE_SERIALIZER_CLASS_CONFIG, JsonSerializer.class);
    // Durability
    config.put(ProducerConfig.ACKS_CONFIG, "all");         // wait for all replicas
    config.put(ProducerConfig.ENABLE_IDEMPOTENCE_CONFIG, true);  // no duplicates
    config.put(ProducerConfig.RETRIES_CONFIG, Integer.MAX_VALUE);
    config.put(ProducerConfig.MAX_IN_FLIGHT_REQUESTS_PER_CONNECTION, 5);
    // Throughput
    config.put(ProducerConfig.BATCH_SIZE_CONFIG, 32768);   // 32KB batch
    config.put(ProducerConfig.LINGER_MS_CONFIG, 5);        // wait 5ms to fill batch
    config.put(ProducerConfig.COMPRESSION_TYPE_CONFIG, "lz4");  // compress batches
    return new DefaultKafkaProducerFactory<>(config);
}

// High-throughput producer (analytics, metrics)
@Bean
public ProducerFactory<String, Object> throughputProducerFactory() {
    Map<String, Object> config = new HashMap<>();
    config.put(ProducerConfig.ACKS_CONFIG, "1");           // only leader ack
    config.put(ProducerConfig.BATCH_SIZE_CONFIG, 65536);   // 64KB batch
    config.put(ProducerConfig.LINGER_MS_CONFIG, 20);       // wait 20ms
    config.put(ProducerConfig.COMPRESSION_TYPE_CONFIG, "snappy");  // fast compression
    return new DefaultKafkaProducerFactory<>(config);
}
```

## Sending Records

```java
@Service
public class OrderEventProducer {
    @Autowired KafkaTemplate<String, OrderEvent> kafkaTemplate;

    public void publishOrderCreated(Order order) {
        OrderEvent event = new OrderEvent(order.getId(), "CREATED", Instant.now());

        // Key = orderId → ensures all events for same order go to same partition
        // This guarantees ordering of events for a single order
        kafkaTemplate.send("orders", order.getId().toString(), event)
            .whenComplete((result, ex) -> {
                if (ex != null) {
                    log.error("Failed to publish order event: {}", order.getId(), ex);
                    // Consider retry or dead-letter queue
                } else {
                    log.debug("Published order {}, partition={}, offset={}",
                        order.getId(),
                        result.getRecordMetadata().partition(),
                        result.getRecordMetadata().offset());
                }
            });
    }
}
```

## Transactions — Exactly-Once Across Topics

```java
// Atomic write to multiple topics
@Transactional
public void publishWithTransaction(Order order) {
    kafkaTemplate.executeInTransaction(ops -> {
        ops.send("orders", order.getId().toString(), new OrderCreatedEvent(order));
        ops.send("inventory", order.getProductId().toString(), new ReserveStockEvent(order));
        ops.send("notifications", order.getUserId().toString(), new NotifyUserEvent(order));
        // All three publish atomically — either all succeed or none do
        return null;
    });
}
```

## Consumer Configuration

```java
@Bean
public ConsumerFactory<String, Object> consumerFactory() {
    Map<String, Object> config = new HashMap<>();
    config.put(ConsumerConfig.BOOTSTRAP_SERVERS_CONFIG, "kafka:9092");
    config.put(ConsumerConfig.GROUP_ID_CONFIG, "order-processing-group");
    config.put(ConsumerConfig.KEY_DESERIALIZER_CLASS_CONFIG, StringDeserializer.class);
    config.put(ConsumerConfig.VALUE_DESERIALIZER_CLASS_CONFIG, JsonDeserializer.class);
    config.put(JsonDeserializer.TRUSTED_PACKAGES, "com.myapp.events");

    // Offset management
    config.put(ConsumerConfig.AUTO_OFFSET_RESET_CONFIG, "earliest"); // start from beginning on new group
    config.put(ConsumerConfig.ENABLE_AUTO_COMMIT_CONFIG, false);      // manual commit

    // Heartbeat and poll interval
    config.put(ConsumerConfig.SESSION_TIMEOUT_MS_CONFIG, 30000);     // 30s before considered dead
    config.put(ConsumerConfig.MAX_POLL_INTERVAL_MS_CONFIG, 300000);  // 5min max between polls
    config.put(ConsumerConfig.MAX_POLL_RECORDS_CONFIG, 50);          // max records per poll

    return new DefaultKafkaConsumerFactory<>(config);
}
```

## @KafkaListener with Manual Commit

```java
@Service
public class OrderConsumer {

    @KafkaListener(
        topics = "orders",
        groupId = "order-processing-group",
        containerFactory = "kafkaListenerContainerFactory"
    )
    public void processOrder(
            ConsumerRecord<String, OrderEvent> record,
            Acknowledgment ack) {
        try {
            log.info("Processing order: {} from partition={}, offset={}",
                record.value().getOrderId(),
                record.partition(),
                record.offset());

            orderService.process(record.value());

            ack.acknowledge();  // commit offset AFTER successful processing
        } catch (RetryableException ex) {
            log.warn("Retryable failure for order {}", record.value().getOrderId(), ex);
            // Don't ack — message will be redelivered
        } catch (Exception ex) {
            log.error("Non-retryable failure for order {}", record.value().getOrderId(), ex);
            ack.acknowledge();  // ack to avoid infinite retry loop
            // Send to dead letter topic for investigation
            deadLetterPublisher.publish("orders.DLT", record);
        }
    }
}
```

## Dead Letter Topic (Spring Kafka Built-in)

```java
@Bean
public ConcurrentKafkaListenerContainerFactory<String, Object> kafkaListenerContainerFactory(
        ConsumerFactory<String, Object> cf) {
    ConcurrentKafkaListenerContainerFactory<String, Object> factory =
        new ConcurrentKafkaListenerContainerFactory<>();
    factory.setConsumerFactory(cf);
    factory.setConcurrency(3);  // 3 consumer threads
    factory.getContainerProperties().setAckMode(ContainerProperties.AckMode.MANUAL);

    // Dead Letter Publishing after 3 retries
    DefaultErrorHandler errorHandler = new DefaultErrorHandler(
        new DeadLetterPublishingRecoverer(kafkaTemplate),
        new FixedBackOff(1000L, 3L)  // retry 3x with 1s delay
    );
    factory.setCommonErrorHandler(errorHandler);
    return factory;
}
```

## Topic Creation with Admin Client

```java
@Configuration
public class KafkaTopicsConfig {

    @Bean
    public NewTopic ordersCreatedTopic() {
        return TopicBuilder.name("orders.created")
            .partitions(12)           // 12 partitions — 12 max parallel consumers
            .replicas(3)              // 3-way replication for fault tolerance
            .config(TopicConfig.MIN_IN_SYNC_REPLICAS_CONFIG, "2")  // 2 must ack
            .config(TopicConfig.RETENTION_MS_CONFIG, String.valueOf(7 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000L))  // 7 days
            .build();
    }

    @Bean
    public NewTopic productStateTopic() {
        return TopicBuilder.name("products.state")
            .partitions(6)
            .replicas(3)
            .compact()  // log compaction — keeps latest value per key
            .build();
    }
}
```

## Key-Based Partitioning

```java
// All events for the same order → same partition → guaranteed ordering
public void sendOrderEvent(Long orderId, OrderEvent event) {
    kafkaTemplate.send(
        "orders.created",
        orderId.toString(),  // KEY → determines partition
        event
    );
}

// Custom partitioner (override default round-robin for specific needs)
@Component
public class PriorityPartitioner implements Partitioner {
    @Override
    public int partition(String topic, Object key, byte[] keyBytes,
                         Object value, byte[] valueBytes, Cluster cluster) {
        int numPartitions = cluster.partitionCountForTopic(topic);
        OrderEvent event = (OrderEvent) value;

        if (event.isPriority()) {
            // Route priority orders to first N/3 partitions — dedicated consumers
            return Math.abs(key.hashCode()) % (numPartitions / 3);
        }
        // Normal orders to remaining partitions
        return (numPartitions / 3) + (Math.abs(key.hashCode()) % (2 * numPartitions / 3));
    }
    // ... onNewBatch, close, configure methods required by interface
}
```

## Partition Count Guidelines

```
Target partitions = max(throughput_target / throughput_per_partition,
                        desired_consumer_parallelism)

Example:
- Target: 10,000 messages/sec
- Throughput per partition: ~1,000 msg/sec (conservative)
- Target parallelism: 8 consumer instances
- Partitions = max(10000/1000, 8) = max(10, 8) = 10 → round up to 12

Practical rule: start with 2-3x your initial consumer count
Allows scaling consumers without repartitioning
```
